               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc>
                     <supportDesc>
                        <support>
                           <p>Volume letter: ka.<lb/>Folio numbers (written out in letters) unclear on most folios. A second set of numbers for pages was added with Tibetan numbers, and yet another (likely on the copy) in Arabic numbers.<lb/>Two folios numbered 12. Two folios numbered 23.<lb/>Some folios are by another hand (e.g., fol. 21, fol. 40, fol. 64) and could belong to another manuscript.<lb/>Lines per folio: 10 and more, with interlinear notes.</p>
                        </support>
                        <extent>110</extent>
                     </supportDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
               </physDesc>
               <history>
                  <provenance>se ra dgon</provenance>
               </history>
               <additional>
                  <adminInfo>
                     <availability>
                        <p>available</p>
                     </availability>
                     <note type="comment">The script and image quality make it difficult do read.&#13;
The manuscript is preserved at Sera monastery ([S635TW6P]: 84).&#13;
&#13;
A post-colophon addition states: dpal ldan nag chung rjes 'brang rgyan kyis mdo' bsal ba'i || ti ka blo 'i mun sel rin cen sgron me 'di..."</note>
